# AI context hygiene — heavy generated previews, not product code
# (OpenCode grep/glob use ripgrep and respect .gitignore automatically;
#  .git is skipped by default. Do NOT create .ignore to exclude — .ignore
#  with ! patterns is for force-INCLUDING back ignored paths.)
icons_check.html
icons_final_check.html
anchor-render-preview.html
trigger-removebg-preview.bmp
panel_mt4_sim.html
panel_mt4_sim*.png
panel_art_proof.html
# The pivot atlas is tracked (it IS the authored content); the single-image
# render is 100% derivable from it via its own export mode, so it is not.
pivot_arrangement_atlas.png
pivot_wall_*.png
**/*.prev
.claude/
.freebuff/
.playwright-mcp/
.sync-test.tmp


# P-BUILD-03: the harnesses in tests/ need the icon tree BESIDE them — MetaEditor
# resolves `#resource "\Files\Icons\x.bmp"` against the SOURCE file's own tree, so
# a harness looks in tests\Files. compile-th3.ps1 creates the junction on demand
# (measured 2026-09-25: without it every icon-bearing module in a harness chain
# fails with 325 x `error 310: resource file ... not found`, while the same
# modules compile green from the repo root). It is a LINK, never repo content.
tests/Files

# P-TH3-REC-06: the labelled samples ARE repo content — the PNG is not an
# attachment, it is the evidence: a rung price is only a claim until it is read
# off the picture beside the candles. MEASURED 2026-10-05: 56 KB per shot, so
# the recorder's full 100-sample cap costs 5.5 MB against GitHub's 1 GB
# recommended ceiling, on a repo that is 22 MB today (<0.5% of the budget). The
# text (Logs\*.txt + the master CSV) rides with it — the numbers and the pixels
# have to stay together or a sample is half a sample. Nothing here is ignored;
# `node tools/th3-dataset-sync.js` pulls new captures in from the terminal.

# P-TH3-DB: the dashboard is a VIEW of Dataset.csv + the sample folders, rebuilt
# by one command (`node tools/th3-dataset-dashboard.js`), and the inline copy
# embeds every PNG as a data URI (1 MB for 20 samples, ~6 MB at the recorder's
# 100-sample cap). Tracking a generated megabyte on every capture is exactly the
# history bloat the samples themselves avoid; the inputs are tracked.
Samples/TH3_Dataset/dashboard.html
Samples/TH3_Dataset/dashboard.inline.html

# Agent scratch: session memory and temp probes. Never repo content.
.workbuddy-ai/
.claude/
.freebuff/

# Token-stack guardrails: heavy/ephemeral dirs never indexed nor committed
.venv/
venv/
target/

# P-GIT-01 (2026-10-02) — SESSION SCRATCH IS NEVER REPO CONTENT. The mirrors, the
# one-off sims and the debug probes a work session leaves behind are how a 91-file
# commit happens: nobody reads them again and they drown the diff that matters.
# Everything here is regenerable (`tools/gen-th3-icons.js` for the icons,
# `tools/sim-*.py` for the mirrors) or belongs to one afternoon's question.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
/tmp-*.html
/tmp-*.js
/tmp-*.png
/tools/tmp-*
/tools/_dbg-*
/-                     # a stray file named "-" (a bad `cmd > -` redirect's output)
